\section{Conventions}{

Each call analyses one observation window, for example a day or an hour.
Unless a function says otherwise, the window has length \code{T = 1} and the
sampling interval is \code{delta_n = 1 / n}, so integrated variances are
expressed per window. Functions whose tuning constants carry time units
take an explicit \code{horizon} argument, which makes those units visible.
}

